==Aftermath==
==='''Political reverberations'''===
==='''Cultural impact'''===
The scandal became a defining event for the Millennial and Flood [[Generation]]s, and a moment that heavily informed the political culture of the latter. Numerous films and series were created immediately after the scandal, with the movie ''Individual 1'' (2021) being the most celebrated in its depiction of the Mueller investigation, and HBO's series ''Steele'' (2022) receiving numerous awards for its depiction of the actual conspiracy between the Trump organization and the Kremlin. Media surrounding the scandal fell out of vogue during the early days of the Flood, with the last major film for nearly a decade, ''The Donald'' (2025), serving as a docudrama of Donald Trump's life, focusing heavily on his rise to the Presidency and his relationship with Russia.

